      "writtenOn": "2025-07-15T14:49:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks, from the log the issue seems to be cpi-\u003eref_framerate going to zero which then causes lc-\u003eavg_frame_size_for_layer to overflow. This doesn\u0027t happen in vp9 because of the function vp9_new_framerate(), which resets for very low framerate.\n\nSimilar function exists in vp8, but it is not called before the temporal layer (lc-\u003e) params are set. Possible fix is here: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/webm/libvpx/+/6733319.",
      "parentUuid": "fb549df0_87eaabdb",
      "revId": "d88b0c86847536b952965a1af4765ffd20d53e23",
